T['agents'][0].update(mechanism='Occupies oestrogen receptors in breast-cancer cells and reduces the growth signals they receive',visual=['Oestrogen can signal through the receptor','Tamoxifen and active breakdown products occupy the receptor','Less oestrogen-driven signalling reaches the cancer cell'],explanation='Tamoxifen is a selective oestrogen-receptor modulator. It blocks the effects of oestrogen in breast tissue but has different effects in some other tissues. Your liver converts it into active forms, including endoxifen. Some medicines affect that conversion, so a pharmacist should review prescriptions, supplements and over-the-counter products.',watch='Ask for help with hot flushes, sleep, mood, sexual symptoms or side effects that make daily doses difficult. Report clot symptoms, unusual vaginal bleeding or new visual changes promptly.')
