T['urgent_extra']='Get urgent help for a swollen painful leg, chest pain, new breathlessness, stroke symptoms, fainting with palpitations, swelling of the face or throat, or a severe blistering rash. Tell the team promptly about unusual vaginal bleeding, visual changes, jaundice, unusual bruising or symptoms that make treatment difficult.'
T['consent_support']='Discuss the expected benefit in your treatment setting alongside clot, womb, eye and liver risks and effects on daily life. Tell the team about previous clots, severe liver disease and all other medicines. Tamoxifen is not contraception: discuss an effective non-hormonal method during treatment and for nine months after stopping, where relevant. Absent periods do not prove infertility. Pregnancy and breastfeeding are excluded from this NCCP pathway. Do not change antidepressants, blood thinners or other regular medicines yourself.'
T['support']=[item('Help with daily treatment','Ask early for help with flushes, sweats, sleep, mood, vaginal or sexual symptoms, nausea or fatigue. A difficult side effect matters even if it is not medically severe. The team can discuss symptom treatment and the endocrine plan.',['nccp','smpc']),item('Support medicines','This oral hormone treatment does not require routine steroid premedication, injections to raise white cells or a standard anti-sickness course. Symptom medicines are chosen individually and checked for interactions.',['nccp','smpc']),item('Bloods, eyes and reviews','Agree who arranges the recommended eye and blood checks, their due windows and who reviews the results. Report bleeding or visual changes between appointments.',['nccp','smpc']),item('Bone and activity','The effect on bone differs before and after menopause. Discuss your own fracture risks and whether a bone-density test is appropriate; activity and bone care should suit your circumstances.',['smpc'])]
T['logistics']['sections'][3]['text']='Review prescriptions, supplements and over-the-counter products, including antidepressants, blood thinners and hormone preparations. Some reduce formation of active endoxifen or add bleeding or heart-rhythm risks. Do not stop an essential medicine yourself; ask oncology pharmacy to reconcile the complete list.'
