clinical={
'00253':{'mechanism':'Selective oestrogen-receptor modulator with antagonist activity in breast tissue and tissue-dependent partial agonism elsewhere. Tamoxifen and active metabolites compete at ER. CYP3A4 mainly forms N-desmethyltamoxifen, which CYP2D6 converts to endoxifen; avoid empiric dose escalation for interactions. Tissue-specific action explains uterine stimulation and differing pre/postmenopausal bone effects.','rationale':'NCCP includes ER-positive adjuvant and advanced disease before or after menopause. Adjuvant duration is an individualized initial/extended endocrine plan; advanced duration depends on response and tolerability. Do not infer prevention, male breast cancer or a modern combination indication from this NCCP card.','monitoring_source_split':{'nccp':'Baseline FBC, renal and LFT. ECG if clinically indicated. Later ophthalmology, INR, LFT and ECG if indicated. Annual gynaecological examination. No universal repeat FBC, calcium or fixed ECG timing is specified in NCCP.','irish_rowex_2026':'Baseline ophthalmology; regular FBC including platelets, LFT and serum calcium, without fixed frequency. ECG/electrolytes guided by QT risk or symptoms.','uk_comparison_only':'Some UK product information specifies a repeat QT-risk ECG at steady state after at least four weeks and contraindicates concurrent anastrozole. These must not be silently attributed to current Irish Rowex/NCCP.'},'organ_function':'NCCP: no expected renal/dialysis adjustment; no mild/moderate hepatic adjustment; severe hepatic impairment not recommended. Do not invent creatinine, AST, bilirubin or generic toxicity dose ladders.','medication_safety':'Avoid potent CYP2D6 inhibitors where possible; CYP3A4 inducer review, no empirical dose increase. Irish Rowex says oestrogen preparations should not be combined and cautions against platelet-aggregation inhibitors; review essential antiplatelets rather than advising abrupt withdrawal. Coumarin potentiation needs careful monitoring; breast-cancer treatment is not the prevention contraindication. Irish AI combination wording is lack of added benefit; preserve sequential switching.','surgery_vte':'NCCP significant prior thromboembolic disease is excluded. Acute/suspected VTE requires urgent management and withholding. Perioperative interruption is individualized to thrombosis risk and cancer-treatment trade-off; no universal stop interval is imposed.','contraception':'Current Irish Rowex/Viatris: effective contraception during and for 9 months after treatment in women; product male advice is 6 months but NCCP00253 scope here is women. Non-hormonal method discussion, pregnancy/BF exclusions, amenorrhoea does not establish infertility.','source_ids':['NCCP00253','HPRA_ROWEX','HPRA_VIATRIS']},
'00361':{'mechanism':'Selective ER degrader: competitive ER antagonism with affinity comparable to oestradiol, reduced ER protein and ER-driven transcription, without the partial agonist activity characteristic of tamoxifen. IM depot provides prolonged absorption; the additional Day15 dose increases exposure during initiation.','rationale':'NCCP00361: postmenopausal ER-positive locally advanced/metastatic disease relapsed/progressed on or after adjuvant anti-oestrogen therapy, ECOG0–2. EMA also contains endocrine-naive and combination indications, which do not broaden this exact monotherapy pathway. Critical visceral disease has not been studied in the EMA caution; this is not a contraindication to every visceral metastasis.','schedule':'500 mg IM on Days1 and15 of cycle1, then Day1 every28days: absolute Days1,15,29,57,85. Two5mL gluteal injections at the usual500mg dose, one in each buttock over1–2minutes each. Separate injection technique and modified-dose plan from standard schedule.','hepatic_source_conflict':'NCCP Table1: Child-PughA no adjustment; B50% of original dose(250mg); Cnot recommended. CurrentEMA: no adjustment mild/moderate with caution; severe contraindicated. Explicitly block numeric recommendation for B and require consultant/pharmacy reconciliation. Current modified dose must not automatically reset to500mg from a renal no-adjustment result.','renal':'CrCl≥30mL/min no adjustment. <30/dialysis no adjustment expected in NCCP but data limited and caution/review required.','injection':'Caution with bleeding diathesis, thrombocytopenia or anticoagulation. No NCCP platelet cutoff or automatic anticoagulant-stop rule. Injection-related neuropathic symptoms require review; use care to avoid sciatic nerve.','monitoring':'Baseline FBC/renal/LFT; repeat LFT when clinically indicated; clinical symptom and individualized disease assessment. No invented routine cycle FBC, QT/echo, DPD, G-CSF or steroid premedication requirements for monotherapy.','assay_interference':'Structural similarity to oestradiol can cause falsely elevated antibody-based oestradiol immunoassay results. Verify assay suitability with laboratory before inferring ovarian activity or endocrine failure.','interaction_scope':'EMA fulvestrant alone needs no adjustment with CYP3A4 inducers/inhibitors. This must not clear capivasertib or CDK4/6 companion interactions; full00947 is a separate pathway.','contraception':'EMA: effective contraception during treatment and for2years after final dose for women of childbearing potential; pregnancy and breastfeeding contraindicated.','source_ids':['NCCP00361','EMA_FASLODEX']}}
save('service-facts.json',{'release':'0.84.20','checked':D,'scope':['00253','00361'],'patient_updates':updates,'clinical_facts':clinical,'integration_notes':['Replace evidence and chapters as entire values so old numerical trial prose is removed. Patient evidence remains qualitative; all numeric trial results belong only in clinician evidence.','Patient updates preserve stable protocol identities, schedule kinds and baseline longitudinal setting-specific follow-up; these are not all new monitoring requirements.','Tamoxifen monitoring distinguishes NCCP from current Irish product supplements; no blanket four-week ECG.','Use full00947 capivasertib/fulvestrant when prescribed;00361 remains monotherapy.','Independent clinical/pharmacy authorization remains outstanding.']})

